      "w": 360,
      "h": 230,
      "comment": {
        "what": "Spawn `codex exec --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox --json -C <workspace> -c model_reasoning_effort=\\\"high\\\" --model gpt-5.5 -`. Use the doc-server cwd as the workspace so AGENTS.md resolution remains correct."
      },
      "facts": [],
      "fields": []
    },
    {
      "id": "queue-session-reuse",
      "title": "One Hour Session Reuse",
      "cardType": "implementation",
      "domainId": "next-features",
      "x": 7843.120457886181,
      "y": 603.3083854129349,
      "w": 360,
      "h": 240,
      "comment": {
        "what": "Persist the real Codex thread id and last trigger timestamp under `.decision-os`. Reuse with `codex exec resume <sessionId>` only when the last trigger is less than one hour old."
      },
      "facts": [],
      "fields": []
    },
    {
      "id": "queue-resume-failure",
      "title": "Resume Failure Recovery",
      "cardType": "implementation",
      "domainId": "next-features",
      "x": 8283.120457886182,
      "y": 603.3083854129349,
      "w": 360,
      "h": 240,
      "comment": {
        "what": "Parse resume failures from stderr and only invalidate the stored session when the error names the active resumed thread. Retry the same queue prompt once as a fresh session."
